A||N||5||Cplensdorf||Remove Tape from side GT windows||||1||
Z||000000||Cplensdorf||07-21-2001||07:47 PM||||What can I use to get the old tape from the side sail windows of my GT without ruining them?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||07-21-2001||08:53 PM||||try the thick edge of a body filler applicator. the yellow rubbery like things. then rub back and forth hard with your fingers. change fingers often, makes them pretty sore. it sorta balls it up and rolls it off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||07-22-2001||11:36 AM||||I used a paint scraper to get as much tape off as I could.  Then I used some of that citri-solv cleaning stuff (smells like oranges!) to moisten the tape and then used a razor blade and the finger rubbing technique.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Took quite a while but ended up being really smooth for when I put new tape on the car to replace the windows.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||07-22-2001||02:00 PM||||A nifty orange-scented chemical called Goo-Away. I think you can find it in office supply stores. Dissolves most tape adhesives, and leaves an orangy-good smell. Not to mention a greasy residue that must be washed off with soapy water  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000004||Toddster||07-22-2001||02:12 PM||||This will piss-off the Mrs. but a long thin sharp steak knife works great! You can get back into the tape without bending the sail panels much. Start at the upper corner near the door, work downwards, then go back to the top and work across pulling lightly as you go. I never go to the pick-and-pull wrecking yard without a sharp steak knife.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cplensdorf||07-22-2001||03:37 PM||||Thanks everyone!!  Well I went ahead and did it before consulting the trusty forum... and behold, I cam to the same conclusion the rest of you have.  Citrus based adhesive remover and a couple layers of skin off of every finger.  Thanks again.||||reg||1
